  "description": "HAWVUA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C144 H128 N10 O10 Sm6,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 4 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 3 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm1F (Sm) has 4 O neighbors; Sm2F (Sm) has 3 O neighbors; Sm3F (Sm) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.505-4.197 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.64-147.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm6O4(cbz)10(thf)6]·2C7H8 (C158H144N10O10Sm6).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
